an rights  tells me the sheer number of calls makes  them think russians are using rape as a  weapon  when a russian soldier rapes a ukrainian  woman a girl a boy an elderly woman they  keep saying things like this will happen  to every nazi [ __ ] or we will rape  until you can't give birth to ukrainians  these are signs of genocide of the  ukrainian people  [Music]  for carina's parents the only certainty  they have is their loss and their fury  we hate the russians  i'm ashamed to speak russian i will  learn ukrainian  they buried karina here in biliterko  near the morgue  two weeks after her 23rd birthday  joining me now is dw's rebecca ritters  who filed that report from ukraine  rebecca welcome you've just spent the  last month  in ukraine can you tell us more about  the evidence that you heard  that suggests russian soldiers are using  rape as a weapon of war  well as the human rights ombuds woman  said in the report they  see the numbers of the of the  testimonies coming in or the calls that  they're receiving  and they're extrapolating and they're  saying that you know obviously this is  systematic uh by those numbers and not  just kind of one-off cases um you know  as you mentioned in the lead into that  report's really difficult to to get  numbers and they're of course expecting  them to grow but one official number  we've heard from the ombudsman's office  is 400 uh 400 calls in the first two  weeks of april but they are expecting  that number to grow they're they're  primarily from the regions around kiev  the capital as as that was liberated in  april and you know when you look at  places like mariupol um they're  expecting to see a lot more cases in  other parts of the country particularly  in those regions uh you know in the time  to come so i think the the number really  speaks to  it being used systematically so  potentially the tip of the iceberg is  there anything being done to protect  women from this  uh it's really difficult to protect  women 